<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Quests</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>quests
quests &lt;word&gt;
</pre>
<p>A quest is a special task someone in the world may ask of you: to find 
something lost, deliver a message, slay a beast or solve a puzzle. Quests 
bring rewards, often after great dangers and hard puzzles: gold, 
experience, a fine item, or entry into a guild. Many guilds ask you to 
finish their quest before you may join (see <a cmd='#'>Help Guilds</a>).
</p><p>There is no list of quests to choose from: you find them by talking to the 
people you meet, listening to what they say, and looking around. The 
newbie guide in Udgaard starts new players on their first one.
</p><p>The quests command lists the quests you have finished, and the ones you 
are on, with a note on each where there is one. Add a word to see only the 
quests with that word in their name: quests guild.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Guilds</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Experience</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Newbie</a>
</pre>




</div>